{"strongs": "H2199", "word": "זָעַק", "translit": "za.aq", "root": "זעק", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "cry, cry out, call", "definition": "[ זָעַק ] verb cry, cry out, call (|| form of צעק q. v.; Arabic , Aramaic ) — Qal Perfect 3 feminine singular וְזָעָ֑קָה 2Sam 13:19 1 singular זָעַקְתִּי Ps 142:6 3 plural זָָֽעֲקוּ Judg 6:7 + 3 t.; וְזָעֲקוּ consecutive Judg 11:11 + 2 t.; 2 masculine plural וּזְעַקְתֶּם consecutive 1Sam 8:18 Imperfect 3 masculine singular יִזְעָ֑ק Isa 15:5 וַיִּזְעַק 1Sam 7:9 + 5 t., etc.; Imperative זְעַק Ezek 21:17 feminine singular זַעֲקְיֿ Isa 14:31 , compare Jer 48:20 Kt ; וְזַעֲקוּ Judg 10:14 + 2 t.; וּזְעָ֑קוּ Jer 48:20 Qr ; Infinitive construct מִזְּעֹק 1Sam 7:8 וְלִזְעֹק 2Sam 19:29 suffix זַעְקֶ֑ךָ Isa 30:19 בְּזַעְקֵךְ Isa 57:13 ( Ol § 245 b Ges «GKC:61»§ 61 . 1. R 1); — 1. call , to one's aid, followed by accusative of person Judg 12:2 . 2. cry, cry out , in need: \\ \\ a. unto God ( ׳ י ), followed by אֶלֿ Judg 3:9 ; Judg 3:15 ; Judg 6:6 ; Judg 6:7 ; Judg 10:10 ; 1Sam 7:8 ; 1Sam 7:9 (+ בעד of intercession), 1Sam 12:8 ; 1Sam 12:10 ; 1Sam 15:11 ; Mic 3:4 ; Jer 11:11 ; Hab 1:2 (with accusative חמס , compare Hos 8:2 below), 2Chr 20:9 ; Ps 22:6 ; Ps 107:13 ; Ps 107:19 ; Ps 142:6 ; Joel 1:14 followed by ׳ אֶליֿ + בְּקוֺל גָּדוֺל Neh 9:4 + קוֺלִי Ps 142:2 (|| התחנן ); + בְּלִבָּם Hos 7:14 (opposed to הֵילִיל ); followed by לְ Hos 8:2 (+ object of words uttered), 1Chr 5:20 followed by suffix Neh 9:28 followed by הַשָּׁמַיִם (without divine name) 2Chr 32:20 (|| התפלל ); absolute, but with implication of cry to ׳ י 1Sam 8:18 ; Isa 30:19 . \\ \\ b. unto other gods, followed by אֶלֿ Judg 10:14 ; Jer 11:12 ; Jonah 1:5 . \\ \\ c. unto king, followed by אֶלֿ 2Sam 19:29 . \\ \\ d. absolute, utterance of horror, anxiety, alarm, distress, sorrow, etc. 1Sam 4:13 ; 1Sam 5:10 ; 1Sam 28:12 (+ בקול גדול ), 2Sam 13:19 ; 2Sam 19:5 (+ קול גדול ), 1Kgs 22:32 = 2Chr 18:31 ; Isa 15:4 ; Isa 26:17 ; Isa 57:13 ; Jer 20:8 (|| קרא , compare Hab 1:2 above), Lam 3:8 (|| אֲשַׁוֵּעַ ) Ezek 9:8 ; Ezek 11:13 ; Ezek 27:30 also of cry heard by God Exod 2:23 ( P ); followed by לְ of that in behalf of, or for which one cries Isa 15:5 ; Jer 48:31 so followed by עַלֿ Jer 30:15 followed by accusative of congnate meaning with verb זְעָקָה Esth 4:1 || היליל Jer 47:2 and especially Imperative Isa 14:31 ; Jer 25:34 ; Jer 48:20 ; Ezek 21:17 . \\ \\ e. cry out against one, followed by עַלֿ Job 31:38 if my land cry out against me (|| יִבְכָּיוּן ); compare also (absolute, and without preposition) Hab 2:11 the stone shall cry out of ( מִן ) the wall . Niph`al Perfect 2 masculine singular נִזְעָ֑קְתָּ Judg 18:23 3 masculine plural נִזְעֲקוּ Judg 18:22 Imperfect וַיִּזָּעֵק Judg 6:34 + 2 t.; וַיִּזָּעֲקוּ Josh 8:16 — be called together ** = be called out for military service, passive of Hiph`il 1. ; compare GFM Judg 18:28 ; assemble, join Josh 8:16 ( J E ), Judg 18:22 ; Judg 18:23 ; 1Sam 14:20 followed by אַחֲרָיו Judg 6:34 ; Judg 6:35 assembled after him , i.e. joined him as his followers. Hiph`il Imperfect וַיַּזְעֵק Judg 4:10 + 3 t.; יַזְעִיקוּ Job 35:9 Imperative הַזְעֶקֿ 2Sam 20:4 Infinitive construct לְהַזְעִיק 2Sam 20:5 — 1. call, call out , or together , for military service, followed by accusative Judg 4:10 ; Judg 4:13 ; 2Sam 20:4 ; 2Sam 20:5 . 2. make a crying Job 35:9 ( יְשַׁוְּעוּ in || clause) 3. have proclamation made ויאמר ׳ ויז Jonah 3:7 . 4. call out to, or at , followed by accusative וַיַּזְעֵק אֹתִי וַיְדַבֵּר Zech 6:8 (si vera lectio; Gr queries וַיָּעַר ?).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2422')\">BDB2422</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2199')\">H2199</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2421')\">BDB2421</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2423')\">BDB2423</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>זָעַק</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>cry, cry out, call</highlightword> (|| form of  <bdbheb><reflink>צעק</reflink></bdbheb> q. v.; Arabic <placeholder1531/>, Aramaic